# AI Idea Studio

AI Idea Studio is a modern idea-to-image and full-video generation application for Wajeeh Codes. It is designed to preserve the original creative idea, expand it into an editable story plan, generate visual references, and support full-video generation workflows with clear provider-based integrations and persistent local storage.

## Features

- Idea editor with project title, description, and editable creative metadata
- Dashboard for viewing, searching, sorting, and managing saved projects
- Persistent storage using SQLite
- AI plan generation fallback with provider-ready extension points
- Image and video generation action endpoints with clear configuration errors when no provider is enabled
- Version history and project status tracking
- Download-ready architecture for generated assets and export metadata

## Tech stack

- Node.js + Express
- SQLite via better-sqlite3
- Static frontend served from `/public`
- Provider interfaces centralized in `services/aiProvider.js`

## Getting started

1. Install dependencies:

   npm install

2. Copy the environment template:

   cp .env.example .env

3. Add the required provider keys if you want real generation:

   - OPENAI_API_KEY for AI plan generation or image APIs
   - STABILITY_API_KEY for image generation
   - RUNWAY_API_KEY or LUMA_API_KEY for video generation

4. Start the app:

   npm run dev

5. Open the app at http://localhost:3000

## Environment variables

See `.env.example` for the full list.

## Important note on generation providers

This repository includes a provider-ready architecture and clear error messaging when no provider is configured. It does not pretend to generate real images or final MP4 assets without a configured provider. The app will explain exactly what to add in `.env` and will otherwise fail cleanly with actionable guidance.

## Project architecture

- `server.js` — Express server and API routes
- `db.js` — SQLite schema and database setup
- `services/aiProvider.js` — generation provider interface and fallback logic
- `public/` — frontend dashboard and editor UI
- `storage/` — persistent asset storage
- `data/` — SQLite database file

## Extending providers

The generation logic is intentionally separated behind `aiProvider` so it can be swapped to OpenAI, Stability, Replicate, Runway, or another provider without changing the dashboard or data model.
